# Architecture Decisions

## Framework
- **Next.js 15**: Server Components reduce client bundle, App Router enables colocation
- **Monorepo: No**: Single app simplicity until proven otherwise

## Database
- **Supabase over raw Postgres**: Built-in auth, realtime, storage, RLS
- **Drizzle over Prisma**: Lighter, SQL-like syntax, better edge support

## Auth
- **Supabase Auth**: Unified with DB, supports OAuth + magic links + RLS
- **Dual roles**: Users have `role: "student" | "tutor" | "both"`

## Real-time Matching
- **Supabase Realtime subscriptions**: Listen to tutor availability changes
- **Presence channel**: Show online tutors, enable instant booking

## Payments
- **Stripe Connect**: Platform model for tutor payouts
- **Escrow pattern**: Hold funds until session confirmed complete

## AI Strategy
- **Tutor matching**: Embed student needs + tutor profiles, vector similarity
- **Study plans**: Generate personalized AP/IB prep schedules
- **Session summaries**: Auto-generate from session notes

## File Structure
- **Feature-based**: `/server/resources/{domain}/` not `/controllers`, `/services`
- **Colocation**: Keep related code together (route + service + schema)

## API Design
- **REST for CRUD**: Simple, cacheable
- **Server Actions for mutations**: Type-safe, no API boilerplate
- **tRPC: No**: Adds complexity, Server Actions sufficient

## State Management
- **Server-first**: RSC + React Query for most data
- **Zustand**: Only for complex client-only state (booking flow wizard)
